{"status":"success","data":[{"site":{"siteid":3411,"sitename":"Sigvalde Träsk","sitedescription":"Small, deep lake, artificially lowered. Physiography: in an area of limestone. Surrounding vegetation: mixture of pine and arable agriculture.","sitenotes":null,"geography":"{\"type\":\"Point\",\"crs\":{\"type\":\"name\",\"properties\":{\"name\":\"EPSG:4326\"}},\"coordinates\":[18.52596,57.34248]}","altitude":27,"collectionunitid":4277,"collectionunit":null,"handle":"SIGVALDE","unittype":"Core","datasets":[{"doi":["10.21233/15ke-zg16"],"agerange":[],"database":"European Pollen Database","datasetid":4419,"datasetpi":[{"initials":"N.-O.","contactid":1265,"firstname":"Nils-Olof","familyname":"Svensson","contactname":"Svensson, Nils-Olof"}],"datasettype":"pollen","datasetnotes":"Number of pollen samples in the dataset match the number of pollen samples in the publication, but the depths are not matching.\r\n\r\nData contributed by Björn E. Berglund.\r\n\r\nMethodology followed Faegri and Iversen (1964) with the following modifications: samples were left to stand in cold HF for several weeks; after acetolysis, clay rich samples sieved through a 7 micrometre sieve.","recdatecreated":"2013-09-30T14:02:42"}]}}],"message":"Retrieved all tables"}